.TH XUR.STD.GUI 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.gui \- desktop GUI with egui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
use std::gui;

gui::run("My App", fn(ui) {
    ui.heading("Welcome");
    if ui.button("Click me") {
        io::println("clicked!");
    }
});
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::gui
provides an immediate-mode GUI backed by
.BR egui / eframe .
Call
.B gui::run
or
.B gui::dialog
with a title and a draw callback; the callback receives a
.B Ui
handle and is called every frame.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B run(title: str, draw: fn(ui)) -> ()
Open a window and run the draw loop until it is closed.
.TP
.B dialog(title: str, draw: fn(ui)) -> ()
Like
.B run
but with a dialog window type hint (X11).
.SH UI METHODS
.TP
.B label(text: str) -> ()
Display a text label.
.TP
.B heading(text: str) -> ()
Display a heading.
.TP
.B small(text: str) -> ()
Display small text.
.TP
.B button(text: str) -> bool
Display a button. Returns
.B true
if clicked this frame.
.TP
.B separator() -> ()
Draw a horizontal separator line.
.TP
.B checkbox(checked: bool, label: str) -> bool
Display a checkbox. Returns the new checked state.
.TP
.B slider_float(label: str, value: float, min: float, max: float) -> float
A float slider. Returns the new value.
.TP
.B slider_int(label: str, value: int, min: int, max: int) -> int
An integer slider. Returns the new value.
.TP
.B text_edit(text: str) -> str
A single-line text input. Returns the new text.
.TP
.B text_edit_multiline(text: str) -> str
A multi-line text input. Returns the new text.
.TP
.B horizontal(body: fn(ui)) -> ()
Lay out children horizontally.
.TP
.B vertical(body: fn(ui)) -> ()
Lay out children vertically.
.TP
.B collapsing(heading: str, body: fn(ui)) -> ()
A collapsible section.
.TP
.B scroll(body: fn(ui)) -> ()
Wrap children in a vertical scroll area.
.TP
.B window(title: str, body: fn(ui)) -> ()
Open a child window (viewport).
.TP
.B dialog(title: str, body: fn(ui)) -> ()
Open a child dialog window.
.TP
.B panel_left(id: str, body: fn(ui)) -> ()
A left side panel.
.TP
.B add_space(amount: float) -> ()
Add vertical spacing.
.SH TEXTURES
A
.B Texture
is an opaque handle to an image the overlay can draw. It is an enum with two
variants:
.B Managed(int)
for an image uploaded to the overlay (e.g.
.BR load_texture_rgba )
and
.B User(int)
for a native game texture registered by an engine module (e.g.
.BR unity::egui::register_texture ).
Scripts normally just hold a
.B Texture
and pass it to
.BR image ;
the variant is only relevant to the backend.
.TP
.B Ctx.load_texture_rgba(name: str, width: int, height: int, rgba: bytes) -> Result<Texture>
Upload raw RGBA8 pixels (length
.BR width*height*4 )
as a managed texture and return its
.BR Texture .
.TP
.B Ctx.free_texture(tex: Texture) -> ()
Release a managed texture. User textures are released through their engine
module's unregister function.
.TP
.B Ui.image(tex: Texture, width: float, height: float) -> ()
Draw a texture at the given size. Handles both
.B Managed
and
.B User
textures.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::gui;
use std::cell;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let count = cell::new(0);

    gui::run("Counter", fn(ui) {
        ui.heading("Counter app");
        ui.label("count: {}".format(count.get()));
        if ui.button("+1") {
            count.set(count.get() + 1);
        }
    });
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
